Materials and methods

Sampling

The sampling area was located in the Kolbudy forest District
(including Pomlewo village and surroundings) which is part           6
of the rural Przywidz commune in Pomeranian Voivodeship,
Poland. The forest contains mixed growths of deciduous and
coniferous trees which are a typical habitat of A. muscaria.
Forest cover was dominated by young, downy birch (Betula
pubescens Ehrh.) interspersed with Scots pine (Pinus
sylvestris L.) and Norway spruce (Picea abies (L.) H.Karst.).
