wiki/sources/cfs2019-organotin-aquatic-hongkong.md:34:**Important note on metals classification:** The analytes in this paper are organotin compounds (TBT, DBT, DOT, TPT), not inorganic tin. Organotin species are distinct from total tin (Sn) in toxicological profile, environmental behavior, and regulatory framework. These compounds enter aquatic food chains primarily through antifouling paints on ships and from agricultural pesticide use; they are endocrine disruptors at very low concentrations (1 ng/L in water for TBT and TPT imposex effects) and are outside the HMTc 10-analyte scope. They are included here under `metals: [Sn]` for element-level routing because they are tin-organic compounds, but synthesis should route the toxicological discussion to [[metals/organotins]] and must not conflate organotins with inorganic Sn.
